    {
      "id": "rust",
      "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/06/26/Rust-1.88.0/",
      "title": "Announcing Rust 1.88.0 | Rust Blog",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "line-1",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "June 26, 2025 · The Rust Release Team\n",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "line-3",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Rust team is happy to announce a new version of Rust, 1.88.0. Rust is a programming language empowering everyone to build reliable and efficient software.\n",
          "start_line": 3,
          "end_line": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "line-5",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "If you have a previous version of Rust installed via rustup, you can get 1.88.0 with:\n",
          "start_line": 5,
          "end_line": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "line-7",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\n$ rustup update stable\n```\n",
          "start_line": 7,
          "end_line": 9
        },
        {
          "id": "line-15",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## What's in 1.88.0 stable\n",
          "start_line": 15,
          "end_line": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "line-17",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Let chains\n",
          "parent_id": "line-15",
          "start_line": 17,
          "end_line": 17
        },
        {
          "id": "line-23",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\nif let Channel::Stable(v) = release_info()\n&& let Semver { major, minor, .. } = v\n&& major == 1\n&& minor == 88\n{\nprintln!(\"`let_chains` was stabilized in this version\");\n}\n```\n",
          "parent_id": "line-17",
          "start_line": 23,
          "end_line": 31
        },
        {
          "id": "line-37",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Naked functions\n",
          "parent_id": "line-15",
          "start_line": 37,
          "end_line": 37
        },
        {
          "id": "line-41",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "For example:\n",
          "parent_id": "line-37",
          "start_line": 41,
          "end_line": 41
        },
        {
          "id": "line-56",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Look for a more detailed post on this soon!\n",
          "parent_id": "line-37",
          "start_line": 56,
          "end_line": 56
        },
        {
          "id": "line-58",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Boolean configuration\n",
          "parent_id": "line-15",
          "start_line": 58,
          "end_line": 58
        },
        {
          "id": "line-64",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "See RFC 3695 for more background!\n",
          "parent_id": "line-58",
          "start_line": 64,
          "end_line": 64
        },
        {
          "id": "line-66",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Cargo automatic cache cleaning\n",
          "parent_id": "line-15",
          "start_line": 66,
          "end_line": 66
        },
        {
          "id": "line-68",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Starting in 1.88.0, Cargo will automatically run garbage collection on the cache in its home directory!\n",
          "parent_id": "line-66",
          "start_line": 68,
          "end_line": 68
        },
        {
          "id": "line-76",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Stabilized APIs\n",
